  "title": "John Locke",
  "summary": "John Locke (1632-1704), born in Wrington in south-west England, was an Oxford academic, physician and political activist. He fled to Holland in 1683, returning in 1689 after the Glorious Revolution. That year he published An Essay Concerning Human Understanding, a founding text of empiricism holding that all our ideas come from experience, and anonymously the Two Treatises of Government, which argues that sovereignty resides in the people. His ideas on limited government were invoked in the American and French revolutions.",
